IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nla-dates`
IMPORT `nla-rules`

-- Limitation Act 1981 (NT) -- the questions of the CLAIMANT.
--
-- SEAT: the individual to whom a cause of action accrues and who brings, or proposes to bring, the action -- the injured
-- person, the worker with a dust disease, the survivor of child abuse, the family member suing for a death, the person
-- defamed, a party to a contract or deed: "By when must I start my action?", "Can I still start it on this day?", "Is
-- there no limit for my abuse or dust disease claim?", "Did their written acknowledgment or payment give me more time?",
-- "Can the court give me more time?", "Can I sue now on an abuse claim dismissed or settled before 15 June 2017?". Two
-- questions (ss 8, 24) are asked by the same individual when answering a claim: a counterclaim, and contribution from
-- another wrongdoer. The court, the putative defendant, an insurer and the Public Trustee get no seat: the court's
-- satisfaction and orders are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of nla-rules.l4. The time
-- bar and the s 39 notice are DEONTIC rules run inside `Can I still commence my action on this day` and `Did my parent or
-- guardian comply with the notice`; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of the Limitation Act 1981 (NT). Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is
-- owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the Northern Territory copyright policy of 8 October 1996; see
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation Act 1981 (NT): the claimant's questions`

§§ `What kind of claim I have`

@export Am I a "person under a disability" under the Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 4, so that my limitation period stops running while it lasts (s 36)? You are if you are under 18, if you cannot manage your affairs in legal proceedings because of age, disease, illness or mental or physical infirmity, or if you are serving a prison sentence after conviction.
GIVEN `am I under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 18 years of age
      `can I not manage legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of age, disease, illness or mental or physical infirmity, you are incapable of managing your affairs in respect of legal proceedings
      `am I serving a prison sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted and are now serving a sentence of imprisonment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a person under a disability` MEANS
    `s 4 -- I am a person under a disability` `am I under 18` `can I not manage legal proceedings` `am I serving a prison sentence`

@export Is my claim for an injury from child abuse one with no limitation period, so I can sue at any time however long ago it happened (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 5A)? It covers damages for personal injury from sexual abuse, serious physical abuse, or psychological abuse arising from either, when you were under 18, including a family's death claim and an estate's claim. A court can still stop a case if a fair trial is impossible.
GIVEN `is it a damages claim for injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for damages for personal injury (in tort, contract, under statute or otherwise), or is a Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 claim for the death, or a claim surviving to the estate
      `what was the abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc What the abuse was: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse arising from sexual or serious physical abuse; or other abuse or harm
      `was I under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 18 when the abuse was perpetrated against you
      `did the injury arise from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the personal injury arose from that abuse
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my claim a child abuse action with no limitation period` MEANS
    `s 5A -- no limitation period applies to my child abuse action` `is it a damages claim for injury` `what was the abuse` `was I under 18` `did the injury arise from it`

@export Is my illness a "dust disease", so that my claim for damages for it has no limitation period (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 12(2)(a), (3))? A dust disease is a pathological condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum that is attributable to dust (for example asbestosis, mesothelioma, silicosis).
GIVEN `is it a condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the illness is a pathological condition of the lungs, the pleura (the lining of the lungs) or the peritoneum (the lining of the abdomen)
      `is it attributable to dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the condition is attributable to dust (for example asbestos or silica dust)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my illness a dust disease` MEANS
    `s 12(3) -- it is a dust disease` `is it a condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum` `is it attributable to dust`

§§ `My time limit`

@export By when must I start my court action, or is there no time limit (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) ss 5, 5A, 9, 12, 14, 17, 36, 38, 39, 41-43, 44AA)? Personal injury, other torts, contracts and money due under a statute: 3 years from when the claim accrued; a Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act claim: 3 years from the death; a deed: 12 years; defamation: 1 year from publication. No limit for child abuse or a dust disease. Time stops while you are under 18 or otherwise under a disability (with 3 years after it ends, at most 30 years), restarts from a written acknowledgment or payment, and waits for fraud or a mistake to be discovered. A time limit in another Act (for example motor accident or workers' compensation) applies instead (s 5).
GIVEN `what kind of action` IS A `Kind of action` @desc What the action is for: damages for personal injury (including disease); another action in tort (including breach of statutory duty); a contract not made by deed; a deed; money recoverable under a statute; a Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 claim for a death; defamation; or land, mortgage, trust, account, judgment, penalty, arbitration award, admiralty, goods, equitable or tax claims (not answered)
      `does another Act set the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act sets a time limit for this kind of action (if so, this Act does not apply: s 5)
      `is it child abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for personal injury arising from child abuse (the answer to the child abuse question)
      `is it a dust disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for damages for personal injury arising from a dust disease (the answer to the dust disease question)
      `day it accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day the cause of action first accrued to you (for most injuries, the day the injury was suffered; for a fatal injuries claim, the day of the death; for defamation, the day of publication, or of first upload for an online publication)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (the person to whom the cause of action accrued)
      `have I died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person to whom it accrued has died (answer for them if you act for their estate)
      `day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day of that death (any date if none)
      `another disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, apart from being under 18, you have been under a disability at a time after the claim accrued: unable to manage your affairs in legal proceedings, or serving a prison sentence after conviction
      `day it began` IS A DATE @desc The day that disability began (any date if none)
      `has it ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that disability has ended
      `day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day it ended (any date if it has not)
      `was a notice to proceed served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you would sue has served a notice to proceed on your court-appointed tutor or guardian (s 38)
      `day of the notice to proceed` IS A DATE @desc The day it was served (any date if none)
      `fraud, concealment or mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is based on fraud or deceit, the claim or the identity of the person liable was fraudulently concealed by the person you sue, or the claim is for relief from the consequences of a mistake
      `has it been discovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you have discovered the fraud, deceit, concealment or mistake, or could have with reasonable diligence
      `day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered it, or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it (any date if not)
      `was it confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you would sue has signed a written acknowledgment of your right, or made you a payment in respect of it (see the confirmation question)
      `day it was confirmed` IS A DATE @desc The day of that acknowledgment or payment (any date if none)
      `was a Public Trustee order made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has appointed the Public Trustee as your tutor after your parent or guardian did not act on a s 39 notice
      `day of the order` IS A DATE @desc The day of that order (any date if none)
      `was a concerns notice given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For defamation: whether you gave the publisher a concerns notice (Defamation Act 2006 s 11A)
      `day of the concerns notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave it (any date if none)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`By when must I commence my action` MEANS
    `the time limit for` (`The claim` WITH
        `claim kind`                    IS `what kind of action`
        `another Act sets the period`   IS `does another Act set the time limit`
        `claim is a child abuse action` IS `is it child abuse`
        `claim is from a dust disease`  IS `is it a dust disease`
        `claim accrual day`             IS `day it accrued`
        `claimant birth day`            IS `my date of birth`
        `claimant has died`             IS `have I died`
        `claimant death day`            IS `day of death`
        `other disability`              IS `another disability`
        `other disability began`        IS `day it began`
        `other disability has ended`    IS `has it ended`
        `other disability ended`        IS `day it ended`
        `notice to proceed served`      IS `was a notice to proceed served`
        `notice to proceed day`         IS `day of the notice to proceed`
        `fraud, concealment or mistake` IS `fraud, concealment or mistake`
        `fraud discovered`              IS `has it been discovered`
        `fraud discovery day`           IS `day it was discovered`
        `confirmed`                     IS `was it confirmed`
        `confirmation day`              IS `day it was confirmed`
        `Public Trustee order made`     IS `was a Public Trustee order made`
        `Public Trustee order day`      IS `day of the order`
        `concerns notice given`         IS `was a concerns notice given`
        `concerns notice day`           IS `day of the concerns notice`)

@export If I start my court action on a given day, is it in time (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) ss 5A, 12, 14, 17, Part III)? Yes on or before the last day of the limitation period, or at any time where none applies; no after it, unless a court extends the time (s 44, or s 44A for defamation).
GIVEN `what kind of action` IS A `Kind of action` @desc What the action is for: damages for personal injury (including disease); another action in tort (including breach of statutory duty); a contract not made by deed; a deed; money recoverable under a statute; a Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 claim for a death; defamation; or land, mortgage, trust, account, judgment, penalty, arbitration award, admiralty, goods, equitable or tax claims (not answered)
      `does another Act set the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act sets a time limit for this kind of action (if so, this Act does not apply: s 5)
      `is it child abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for personal injury arising from child abuse (the answer to the child abuse question)
      `is it a dust disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for damages for personal injury arising from a dust disease (the answer to the dust disease question)
      `day it accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day the cause of action first accrued to you (for a fatal injuries claim, the day of the death; for defamation, the day of publication)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (the person to whom the cause of action accrued)
      `have I died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person to whom it accrued has died (answer for them if you act for their estate)
      `day of death` IS A DATE @desc The day of that death (any date if none)
      `another disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, apart from being under 18, you have been under a disability at a time after the claim accrued: unable to manage your affairs in legal proceedings, or serving a prison sentence after conviction
      `day it began` IS A DATE @desc The day that disability began (any date if none)
      `has it ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that disability has ended
      `day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day it ended (any date if it has not)
      `was a notice to proceed served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you would sue has served a notice to proceed on your court-appointed tutor or guardian (s 38)
      `day of the notice to proceed` IS A DATE @desc The day it was served (any date if none)
      `fraud, concealment or mistake` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is based on fraud or deceit, the claim or the identity of the person liable was fraudulently concealed by the person you sue, or the claim is for relief from the consequences of a mistake
      `has it been discovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you have discovered the fraud, deceit, concealment or mistake, or could have with reasonable diligence
      `day it was discovered` IS A DATE @desc The day you discovered it, or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it (any date if not)
      `was it confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you would sue has signed a written acknowledgment of your right, or made you a payment in respect of it
      `day it was confirmed` IS A DATE @desc The day of that acknowledgment or payment (any date if none)
      `was a Public Trustee order made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court has appointed the Public Trustee as your tutor after your parent or guardian did not act on a s 39 notice
      `day of the order` IS A DATE @desc The day of that order (any date if none)
      `was a concerns notice given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For defamation: whether you gave the publisher a concerns notice (Defamation Act 2006 s 11A)
      `day of the concerns notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave it (any date if none)
      `day I commence` IS A DATE @desc The day you file (or would file) the originating process starting the action
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still commence my action on this day` MEANS
    `the action can be commenced on` `day I commence` `for` (`The claim` WITH
        `claim kind`                    IS `what kind of action`
        `another Act sets the period`   IS `does another Act set the time limit`
        `claim is a child abuse action` IS `is it child abuse`
        `claim is from a dust disease`  IS `is it a dust disease`
        `claim accrual day`             IS `day it accrued`
        `claimant birth day`            IS `my date of birth`
        `claimant has died`             IS `have I died`
        `claimant death day`            IS `day of death`
        `other disability`              IS `another disability`
        `other disability began`        IS `day it began`
        `other disability has ended`    IS `has it ended`
        `other disability ended`        IS `day it ended`
        `notice to proceed served`      IS `was a notice to proceed served`
        `notice to proceed day`         IS `day of the notice to proceed`
        `fraud, concealment or mistake` IS `fraud, concealment or mistake`
        `fraud discovered`              IS `has it been discovered`
        `fraud discovery day`           IS `day it was discovered`
        `confirmed`                     IS `was it confirmed`
        `confirmation day`              IS `day it was confirmed`
        `Public Trustee order made`     IS `was a Public Trustee order made`
        `Public Trustee order day`      IS `day of the order`
        `concerns notice given`         IS `was a concerns notice given`
        `concerns notice day`           IS `day of the concerns notice`)

§§ `More time: acknowledgment, the court, amendment`

@export Did the other side's acknowledgment or payment restart my limitation period (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) ss 40(1)(e), 41)? Only a written, signed acknowledgment of your right, or a payment in respect of it, made to you (or someone you claim through) by the person liable, before the period expired. The period then counts afresh from that day.
GIVEN `what did they give` IS A `Kind of confirmation` @desc What you received: a written acknowledgment of your right signed by its maker; a payment in respect of your right; an acknowledgment not in writing or not signed; a notice to proceed under s 38 or 39; or nothing of that kind
      `was it made to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was made to you, or to a person through whom you claim
      `was it made by the person I would sue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was made by the person you would sue, or by someone whose liability has passed to that person (for example on death)
      `day it was made` IS A DATE @desc The day it was made
      `day my claim accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day your cause of action accrued (or the limitation period began to run)
      `last day of my period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of your limitation period without the acknowledgment or payment (the answer to the time limit question)
GIVETH A `Confirmation effect`
`Did their acknowledgment or payment restart my time` MEANS
    `s 41 -- what the confirmation does` `what did they give` `was it made to me` `was it made by the person I would sue` `day it was made` `day my claim accrued` `last day of my period`

@export Can the court extend the time for starting my action (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 44)? Not for defamation. For a limitation period set by this Act, only if the court is satisfied either that facts material to your case were learnt in the last 12 months of the period or after it and you sued within 12 months of learning them, or that the defendant's representations or conduct reasonably led you not to sue in time; and that it is just. For a time limit set by another Act, the court may extend as it thinks fit.
GIVEN `is it defamation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the action is for defamation (s 44 does not apply; see the defamation extension question)
      `is there a limitation period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a time limit applies at all (answer no for child abuse or dust disease claims)
      `is it set by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the time limit is set by the Limitation Act 1981 itself (answer no if another Act or instrument sets it)
      `last day of my period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the limitation period (the answer to the time limit question)
      `did I learn material facts late` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there were facts material to your case that you did not ascertain until late (in the last 12 months of the period, or after it)
      `day I learnt them` IS A DATE @desc The day you ascertained those facts (any date if none)
      `day I start the action` IS A DATE @desc The day you started, or will start, the action
      `does the court find them material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied those facts were material to your case (the court's judgment)
      `did the defendant lead me not to sue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that your failure to sue in time resulted from representations or conduct of the defendant (or someone you reasonably believed acted for them) and was reasonable (the court's judgment)
      `does the court find it just` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that in all the circumstances it is just to extend the time (the court's judgment)
GIVETH A `Court extension`
`Can the court extend my time` MEANS
    `s 44 -- the court may extend` `is it defamation` `is there a limitation period` `is it set by this Act` `last day of my period` `did I learn material facts late` `day I learnt them` `day I start the action` `does the court find them material` `did the defendant lead me not to sue` `does the court find it just`

@export For my defamation claim, can the court extend the 1-year limitation period, and to when (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) ss 44A, 44C)? Up to 3 years from the publication, if you satisfy the court it is just and reasonable to let the action proceed, even after the year has run; otherwise not at all.
GIVEN `day of publication` IS A DATE @desc The day the matter was published (for an online publication, the day it was first uploaded or sent)
      `is the court satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you satisfy the court that it is just and reasonable to allow the action to proceed (the court's judgment, having regard to your delay, its reasons and the evidence lost)
GIVETH A `Defamation extension`
`Can the court extend my defamation time` MEANS
    `s 44A -- the defamation extension` `day of publication` `is the court satisfied`

@export If the limitation period expired after I started my proceeding, must the court let me amend my documents (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 48A)? Yes where the court would otherwise allow the amendment and is satisfied no other party would suffer prejudice that an adjournment or costs could not meet; the section does not apply to proceedings started before 1 November 1987.
GIVEN `day my proceeding started` IS A DATE @desc The day your proceeding was commenced
      `would the court otherwise allow it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court would allow the amendment but for the limitation period having expired
      `is the court satisfied there is no prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that no other party would be prejudiced by the amendment in a way that could not be met by an adjournment, costs or otherwise (the court's judgment)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the court allow my amendment` MEANS
    `s 48A -- the court must allow my amendment` `day my proceeding started` `would the court otherwise allow it` `is the court satisfied there is no prejudice`

§§ `A notice served on my parent or guardian while I am under 18 (only if the person I would sue has served a s 39 notice)`

@export The person I would sue served a notice on my parent or guardian under s 39: by when must they bring my action (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 39(1))? Within 6 months after the notice was served.
GIVEN `day the notice was served` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice was served on your parent or guardian
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my parent or guardian bring my action under the notice` MEANS
    `s 39 -- the last day under the notice` `day the notice was served`

@export Did my parent or guardian comply with the s 39 notice (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 39(1), (2))? If they did not bring the action within 6 months, the person you would sue may ask the Supreme Court to appoint the Public Trustee as your tutor; your own limitation period is then at least 3 years from that order.
GIVEN `day the notice was served` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice was served on your parent or guardian
      `day the action was brought` IS A DATE @desc The day your parent or guardian brought (or will bring) the action for you as guardian ad litem
GIVETH A `Notice outcome`
`Did my parent or guardian comply with the notice` MEANS
    `s 39 -- the outcome of the notice` `day the notice was served` `day the action was brought`

§§ `When I am being sued (only if a claim has been brought against me)`

@export I am being sued and want to counterclaim or set off: when is my counterclaim taken to have been started, for the time limit (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 8)? On the day the action against you was started, as a separate action.
GIVEN `day the action against me started` IS A DATE @desc The day the action in which you plead the counterclaim or set-off was commenced
GIVETH A DATE
`When is my counterclaim taken to be commenced` MEANS
    `s 8 -- the day my counterclaim is taken to be commenced` `day the action against me started`

@export I was held liable (or agreed to pay) for damage another wrongdoer also caused: by when must I sue them for contribution (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 24)? By the earlier of 2 years from the judgment, award or agreement fixing your liability and 4 years from the end of the limitation period for the injured person's own action.
GIVEN `day my liability was fixed` IS A DATE @desc The day of the judgment or arbitral award against you for the damage, or, if none, of the agreement fixing the amount you were liable to pay
      `did the injured person's action have a time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person's own action had a limitation period (answer no for a child abuse or dust disease claim)
      `last day of their period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the injured person's limitation period (any date if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I sue for contribution` MEANS
    `s 24 -- the last day for contribution` `day my liability was fixed` `did the injured person's action have a time limit` `last day of their period`

§§ `Child abuse claims dismissed or settled before 15 June 2017 (only if there was an earlier action or settlement)`

@export My child abuse claim was dismissed as out of time, settled or still running before 15 June 2017: can I sue now (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) ss 53-55)? Yes despite a judgment that the claim was out of time (or a professional negligence judgment on that ground), as if the earlier action had not been started; not where a court finally decided the matter on other grounds.
GIVEN `is it a child abuse claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for personal injury arising from child abuse (the answer to the child abuse question)
      `what happened before 15 June 2017` IS A `Earlier outcome` @desc What happened before 15 June 2017: nothing; a judgment that the limitation period had expired; a judgment on your legal professional negligence claim on that ground; a judgment finally deciding the matter on other grounds; a settlement made because the claim was out of time; a settlement made for other reasons; or an action you had started that was still undecided then
GIVETH A `Where Part V leaves my claim`
`Can I sue now on my child abuse claim decided before 15 June 2017` MEANS
    `ss 53-55 -- where Part V leaves my claim` `is it a child abuse claim` `what happened before 15 June 2017`

@export Can this court set aside the earlier judgment that my child abuse claim was out of time (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 54(5)-(7))? Only if it considers it just and reasonable; the Supreme Court can do so on application even if not hearing the action; another court can set aside only its own judgment, and only while hearing your action.
GIVEN `is it the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are asking the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory
      `is it hearing my action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that court is hearing your new action
      `was the judgment its own` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the earlier judgment was given by that same court
      `does it consider it just` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court considers it just and reasonable to set the judgment aside (the court's judgment)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can this court set aside the earlier judgment` MEANS
    `s 54(5)-(7) -- the court may set aside the earlier judgment` `is it the Supreme Court` `is it hearing my action` `was the judgment its own` `does it consider it just`
